Algorithm 1 BRANCH-SOLVE-MERGE: LLM Program for LLM Evaluation   
Require: Question $q$ , LLM Responses $\{r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}\}$ , Modules $m = \{\text{branch}(\cdot), \text{solve}(\cdot), \text{merge}(\cdot)\}$ function BSM(q, $r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}, m$ , swap) $C \leftarrow$ branch(q)  
for each $c_i \in C$ do  
if swap = False then $s_i^{(A)}, s_i^{(B)} \leftarrow \text{solve}(q, r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}, c_i)$ else $s_i^{(A)}, s_i^{(B)} \leftarrow \text{solve}(q, r^{(B)}, r^{(A)}, c_i)$ end if  
end for $y^{(A,B)} \leftarrow \text{merge}(q, \{c_i\}_{i=1}^k, \{s_i^{(A)}\}_{i=1}^k, \{s_i^{(B)}\}_{i=1}^k)$ return $y^{(A,B)}$ end function  
function BRANCH-SOLVE-Merge(q, $r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}, m$ ) $y^{(A,B)} = \text{BSM}(q, r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}, m, \text{swap} = \text{False})$ $y^{(B,A)} = \text{BSM}(q, r^{(A)}, r^{(B)}, m, \text{swap} = \text{True})$ if $y^{(A,B)} = A$ & $y^{(B,A)} = B$ then $y \leftarrow A$ else if $y^{(A,B)} = B$ & $y^{(B,A)} = A$ then $y \leftarrow B$ else $y \leftarrow \text{tie}$ end if  
return y  
